{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2457","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2457","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2457\",\"parent_revision\":\"3813c0ac0899e4f8decd9aaba5b45176b0539ef7867eb0ae7af9816b6fff9eee\",\"root_revision\":\"3813c0ac0899e4f8decd9aaba5b45176b0539ef7867eb0ae7af9816b6fff9eee\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWhen T5 was set to `skipped` via `sam_task(action='state', status='skipped')`, `sam_plan(action='ready')` returned `{\\\"ready_tasks\\\": [], \\\"count\\\": 0}` and `sam_plan(action='status')` showed `\\\"blocked_tasks\\\": [{\\\"T6\\\": [\\\"T5\\\"]}]`. T6 remained blocked. The only path forward was to claim T6 directly via `sam_task(action='claim')`, bypassing the readiness system.\\n\\nThe `complete-implementation` skill instructs setting T5 (Documentation Update) to `skipped` when T4 (Documentation Drift Audit) finds no drift, then continuing to T6 (Context Refinement). T6 depends on T5. After T5 was set to `skipped`, the SAM backend treated it as a non-terminal state for dependency resolution: T6 never became ready via `sam_plan(action='ready')`.\\n\\n`skipped` is a permitted status value \u2014 it appears in the skip whitelist in the `complete-implementation` Completion Verification Gate \u2014 but the dependency resolver does not treat it as terminal.\\n\\nObserved: QG plan P49573878, T5\u2192T6 dependency, session 2026-05-25. Affected: every `complete-implementation` run where T4 finds no documentation drift.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **sam skipped task status does not satisfy dependency checks \u2014 downstream tasks remain blocked** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-05-25 \u2014 complete-implementation run for issue #2437\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"99310114854f0690dcf7a76d3bf0b79d276328e29db262b9a903c4f01ee279c8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCPurA\"}"}